  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Prince Feng Xian praises Feng Jiu Ge’s transformation: the outer appearance is flawless, and the disguised dao marks really resemble sword path dao marks, with an aura no different from any Northern Plains Gu Immortal.",
      "chapters": [
        744
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_prince_feng_xian",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After a sword light empties five to six li of sea, lingering sword path dao marks are extremely overbearing. They block the water path dao marks and prevent the water from filling the gap.",
      "chapters": [
        956
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lingering-sea-trench",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sword light damage is extremely troublesome: its sword path dao marks seem to contain a corrosive nature. Remaining parts of Heaven Overseeing Tower may still stand, but they will not last for long if the marks keep corroding.",
      "chapters": [
        957
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "corrosive-sword-light",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even as an immortal zombie with a destroyed immortal aperture, Bo Qing still has his sword path dao marks. The higher a Gu Immortal’s cultivation, the more dao marks they have, and the same Immortal Gu produces different outcomes when amplified by different mark counts. Qin Bai Sheng has not a single sword path dao mark, yet five finger fist heart sword lets him fight Feng Jiu Ge on equal grounds; Bo Qing’s vast sword path dao marks let him almost replicate the glory he had when alive.",
      "chapters": [
        962
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "amplifying-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bo_qing",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "char_qin_bai_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every sword light from Bo Qing contains sword path dao marks. After the light lands, those marks are carved into the valley, creating a special location where many wild sword path Gu worms are slowly produced.",
      "chapters": [
        1059
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
